-- title:
--   Finiteness over K(t) for every transcendental t
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, and let $x \in F$ be an element such that $F$ is finite-dimensional as a vector space over the intermediate field $K(x) =$ `IntermediateField.adjoin K {x}`. Let $t \in F$ be transcendental over $K$, that is, $t$ is not algebraic over $K$ (`Transcendental K t`). The conclusion is that $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(t) =$ `IntermediateField.adjoin K {t}`. The hypothesis on $x$ is an instance assumption, and no relation between $x$ and $t$ is required: $x$ is an arbitrary element witnessing finiteness over some simple intermediate extension, and the assertion is that finiteness then holds over the subfield generated by any transcendental element. (If $x$ happens to be algebraic over $K$ the hypothesis forces $F$ to be algebraic over $K$, so no transcendental $t$ exists and the statement is empty; the substantive case is $F$ a function field in one variable over $K$.)
--
--   This is the intermediate-field form of the standard fact that a function field of one variable is finite over $K(t)$ for every $t$ transcendental over the constant field, independently of the chosen generator. It is used throughout the curve-theoretic part of the development, for instance in the treatment of reductions and of places, where a transcendental element is produced by other means and finiteness over the field it generates is then needed.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_finiteDimensional_adjoin_of_transcendental.lean

import Mathlib.FieldTheory.IntermediateField.Adjoin.Defs
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Algebraic.Defs
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FiniteDimensional.Defs

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem AlgebraicCurve.finiteDimensional_adjoin_of_transcendental {K F : Type*} [Field K] [Field F] [Algebra K F] (x : F)
    [FiniteDimensional (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({x} : Set F)) F] {t : F} (ht : Transcendental K t) :
    FiniteDimensional (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({t} : Set F)) F := by sorry
